OVERVIEW: Wrap a video bitstream in a DICOM Video IOD

USAGE: dicom-video convert [<options>] <input> --output <output>

ARGUMENTS:
  <input>                 Input video file: H.264/HEVC in an MP4 or MPEG-2
                          Transport Stream container (PS3.5 8.2.7-8.2.11);
                          MPEG-2 video in MP4, an MPEG-2 Program Stream, PES or
                          elementary stream (8.2.5, 8.2.6: container not
                          constrained); MOV is probed but not converted

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output DICOM file path
  --type <type>           Video type: endoscopic, microscopic or photographic
                          (values: endoscopic, microscopic, photographic)
  --transfer-syntax <transfer-syntax>
                          Transfer Syntax UID (auto-detected by default): an
                          MPEG2, MPEG-4 AVC/H.264 or HEVC/H.265 UID of PS3.6
                          Table A-1; a UID not registered there is refused
                          (exit 1)
  --frame-rate <frame-rate>
                          Override the probed frame rate (validated)
  --instance-number <instance-number>
                          Instance Number (default: 1) (default: 1)
  --series-number <series-number>
                          Series Number (default: 1) (default: 1)
  --dry-run               Probe and validate only; write nothing
  --trust-input           Encapsulate a transport stream without validating it
  --force                 Overwrite the output file if it exists
  -v, --verbose           Show the reasoning behind each step
  --patient-name <patient-name>
                          Patient's Name, in DICOM caret form (e.g. Doe^Jane)
  --patient-id <patient-id>
                          Patient ID
  --patient-birth-date <patient-birth-date>
                          Patient's Birth Date (YYYYMMDD); other forms are
                          refused (exit 1, VR DA)
  --patient-sex <patient-sex>
                          Patient's Sex (M, F or O); other values are refused
                          (exit 1, PS3.3 Table C.7-1)
  --study-uid <study-uid> Study Instance UID (generated if not given)
  --series-uid <series-uid>
                          Series Instance UID (generated if not given)
  --accession-number <accession-number>
                          Accession Number
  --study-id <study-id>   Study ID
  --referring-physician <referring-physician>
                          Referring Physician's Name
  --series-description <series-description>
                          Series Description
  --modality <modality>   Modality (overrides the video type's default; PS3.3
                          A.32.5-A.32.7 require ES endoscopic, GM microscopic,
                          XC photographic); any other value is refused (exit 1)
  --strict-modality       Reject a --modality value that is not a current DICOM
                          Defined Term
  --manufacturer <manufacturer>
                          Manufacturer
  --institution-name <institution-name>
                          Institution Name
  --audio-channel-source <audio-channel-source>
                          Source of the multiplexed audio (PS3.16 CID 3000): a
                          keyword or SCHEME:VALUE[:MEANING] (the CID is
                          Extensible; MEANING is required for a code that is
                          not listed). Given once, it applies to every audio
                          track; repeated, it gives one source per audio track
                          in container order, and a count that does not match
                          the tracks exits 1. It is written as the Channel
                          Source Sequence (003A,0208) of each Multiplexed Audio
                          Channels Description Code Sequence (003A,0300) Item
                          (PS3.3 Table C.7-13: one Item per channel, each with
                          its own source); without it that sequence has no
                          Items. Keywords: voice, operators-narrative,
                          ambient-room-environment, doppler-audio,
                          phonocardiogram, physiological-audio-signal
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

